error[NK1202]: `line.len() > 0` is a claim about data from outside the program.
  --> tests/a_line_read_from_standard_input_is_data_from_outside.nika:9:5
   |
 9 |     assert(line.len() > 0)
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: `line` comes from outside the program, so nothing the compiler can see says what it holds.
   = note: That it is wrong is a case the program has to handle, not a defect an `assert` catches.
   = help: Check it where it arrives, with a guard the program handles: `throw BadInput(line) if !(line.len() > 0)`, or `return … if !(line.len() > 0)`. After that line, this `assert` is proved.
